From 0d924200b985abdb1b2c367d00b5f9e781697eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 80/81] misc: fastrpc: Do not restart invocations when the
 system suspends

User space invocations wait interruptibly for the reply of the DSP. The
freezer wakes such a task with a fake signal, the wait returns
-ERESTARTSYS and the system call is restarted on resume. The context of
the first attempt stays pending, so the DSP receives the same invocation
twice.

For a daemon that serves the DSP (adsp_listener next2) the second
invocation carries the result of the previous request again. On the
OnePlus 8 Pro the sensor DSP takes an exception in its FastRPC thread at
every resume:

  PDM: service 'sensor_process' crash: 'EX:sensor_process:0x1:frpc_dsp:0x73:PC=0xb20955ac'
  remoteproc remoteproc0: crash detected in slpi: type fatal error

Make the wait freezable, so that the task is frozen in place and simply
continues to wait after resume.

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/misc/fastrpc.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index 8a2a5414f..94657dccf 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1278,7 +1278,13 @@ static int fastrpc_internal_invoke(struct fastrpc_user *fl,  u32 kernel,
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/*
+		 * Freezable: the freezer otherwise interrupts the wait, the
+		 * system call is restarted on resume and sends the invocation
+		 * a second time while the first one is still pending.
+		 */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	if (err)
